  ],
  "text": "You used AI about twenty times today, and almost none of it looked like a chatbot. The word makes people picture a conversation. Most of it never says a word. Autocorrect guessed what you meant, from what people usually mean. Your maps app predicted traffic that has not happened yet, and routed you around it. Your inbox sorted spam from post using a model nobody wrote rules for. And the biggest one is in your pocket, inside every photograph you take. Night mode is a stack of frames combined by a model deciding what ought to be sharp. Your bank ran a fraud model on your card before the payment had finished. None of that is new, and none of it announced itself. AI stopped being a topic years ago and became plumbing. The chatbots are the visible part. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
